<title>USA: Chrysler recalls 675,000 '91-'92 vehicles.</title>
<headline>Chrysler recalls 675,000 '91-'92 vehicles.</headline>
<dateline>AUBURN HILLS, Mich. 1997-01-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>Chrysler Corp said Tuesday it is recalling about 675,000 of its 1991 and 1992 model-year minivans, Dodge Shadow and Plymouth Sundance vehicles to inspect them for steering wheel cracks.</p>
<p>It said the recall includes Chrysler, Dodge and Plymouth brand minivans produced from January 1991 through June 1992. Plymouth Sundance and Dodge Shadow 1991 and 1992 models in the recall include those with four-cylinder engines and manual transmissions, produced from July 1990 through June 1992.</p>
<p>Chrysler said in rare instances, cracks may occur in the steering wheel due to metal fatigue.</p>
<p>((-- Chicago newsdesk 312 408-8787))</p>
